Right. So I was in pakistan as the as the chief of counterterrorism operations there

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:27.510
And we had caught up as a beta on the night of march 22nd and not just mark, but not just I was a beta

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:29.510
but

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:38.710
I'm not allowed to say the number still but it's many dozens of al-qaeda fighters and three or four senior al-qaeda leaders camp commanders

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:45.670
And so on I finished my tour in pakistan. I went back to headquarters and on the strength of that

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:51.910
I got promoted. I got a medal. I got a promotion. I got an amazing onward job

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.430
So I was in a cafeteria one day

00:08:56.390 --> 00:09:03.030
And one of my colleagues who was a senior counterterrorism officer came up to me in the cafeteria and he said

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:07.990
Oh, hey, I'm glad I ran into you. I wanted to ask you and he said this very casually

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:12.950
